From: Tilo <tilo@tilo.so>
Subject: virtio-gpu: do not block a dumb flush on a 50 ms fence

The synchronous dirtyfb commit waits up to 50 ms for a fence allocated
in the same flush, after that flush has already been sent to the host.
When the host does not signal the fence, every virtual present stalls
for that timeout. The compositor then schedules the next paint one
refresh past the late retirement, about 67 ms after the previous one.

The atomic commit still waits for the CRTC vblank timer. The driver
keeps its own fence reference until the host signals it.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -224,8 +224,11 @@ static void virtio_gpu_resource_flush(struct drm_plane *plane,
 					      width, height, objs,
 					      vgplane_st->fence);
 		virtio_gpu_notify(vgdev);
-		dma_fence_wait_timeout(&vgplane_st->fence->f, true,
-				       msecs_to_jiffies(50));
+		/*
+		 * The flush is already queued. Waiting out this fence blocks the
+		 * guest's atomic commit for 50 ms when the host does not signal it.
+		 * The commit's vblank wait is the refresh clock.
+		 */
 	} else {
 		virtio_gpu_cmd_resource_flush(vgdev, bo->hw_res_handle, x, y,
 					      width, height, NULL, NULL);
